{"_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": ""}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "Types of Storage"}, {"type": "position", "content": 5}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 1}, {"type": "level", "content": "B1.2"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you hear and use to talk about types of storage."}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Build the user interface, supported on the prototype assessment, determining the inputs and outputs required in the design and defining the navigation guidelines, according to the user's needs. Identifies different hardware components and peripheral devices."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Discusses a range of options for potential actions at work through the correct use of grammar, vocabulary; level of formality and purpose, and cohesion and coherence aspects appropriate to this level.  Exchanges simple information on the hardware devices and the architecture of a system to create the IT solution."}], "type": "objectives"}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "enpe8n6le01ob05re1img01.jpg"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "floppy disk"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "plastic and portable device used to transport files"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: The most common device was the floppy disk but now we have hard drives."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n6le01ob05aud01"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "format"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "the coding in which something is designed"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: They can handle a high-capacity storage in different formats."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n6le01ob05aud02"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "desktop"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "something that can fit on a desk"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: You can use them in laptops or desktop computers."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n6le01ob05aud03"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "expand"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to make something bigger in capacity"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb) "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Cloud storage, which is related to an online service with a network memory that you can expand.  "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n6le01ob05aud04"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "volatile"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a device that does not retain data when it is powered off"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Volatile memories are intended to clear all data when the power gets off."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n6le01ob05aud05"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "non-volatile"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a device that retains data even if it is powered off"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: All of them were designed as non-volatile memories."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n6le01ob05aud06"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "a)\tLook for information about optical and magnetic storage systems."}, {"type": "text", "content": "b)\tChoose 3 devices of each one of them."}, {"type": "text", "content": "c)\tDraw the devices that you have chosen."}, {"type": "text", "content": "d)\tWrite a description for each device and share your descriptions and pictures with your partners."}], "type": "takeaway_extension"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "\u274f\tI search information about optical and magnetic storage."}, {"type": "text", "content": "\u274f\tI write a description for each device."}, {"type": "text", "content": "\u274f\tI share my product with my partners. "}], "type": "takeaway_assessment"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Simple Past Passive- (Affirmative Form.)"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You use <span class=\"strong\"> Simple Past Passive </span> to provide more importance to the object and a past action in a sentence rather than the subject"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"strong\"> Simple past Passive </span> is used when the subject of the sentence can be omitted since it is implicit in the message. On the other hand, to mention the subject you have to use the preposition <span class=\"strong\"> by </span> followed by the noun. <br/><br/> Let's compare these two sentences: <br/><br/> <span class=\"strong\"> Active voice:</span> <br/> <li><span class=\"italic\"> People </span> used floppy disks to back up and transport data. </span><span class=\"strong\"> </li>  <br/><br/>  <span class=\"strong\"> Passive voice:</span> <br/> <li><span class=\"italic\"> Floppy disks </span> were used (by people) to back up and transport data. </span><span class=\"strong\">  </li> <br/><br/> As you can see, in passive voice the subject of the sentence \u201cpeople\u201d is not necessary; therefore, omitted.  <br/><br/>  Grammar structure for passive voice:  <br/><br/> <div class=\"center_text\"> Object of the sentence + <span class=\"strong\"> Past of be </span> + Verb in past participle + Complement + (agent).</div> <br/><br/>  Example:  <br/> <li><span class=\"italic\"> Different types of storage devices <span class=\"strong\"> were </span> designed for individual needs. </span> </li>"}, {"type": "example", "content": "All of them were designed as non-volatile memories due to the fact that volatile memories are intended to clear all data when the power gets off."}, {"type": "example", "content": "Discs were created to read and write information through a laser.  "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Disks were made for magnetic storage."}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Types of Storage."}, {"type": "describer", "content": "There are different <span class=\"strong\"> types of storage </span> that can be classified into four categories. Magnetic, optical, solid state, and cloud storage. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "In the past, floppy disks were very common as a mean of storage. However, their storage capacity was very limited and their structure was fragile. On the other hand, hard disks have been evolving with time, nowadays we can find portable units with a large amount of space.  <br/><br/> CDs have also been reformed in order to obtain various benefits. We can find different formats such as CD-DA (Digital Audio), CD-ROM (for computer programs), CD-R (Recordable), and CD-RW (rewritable). Besides the previous mentioned, we also have devices such as flash drives or cloud drives on the internet that have allowed us to transport and access information easier. "}], "type": "learning_points"}], "type": "sena", "labs": [{"stimuli": [{"template_override": 1, "_data": [], "type": "welcome", "id": 0, "contents": [{}]}, {"template_override": 1, "contents": [{"value": {"images": [{"time": "100", "image": "enpe8n6le01ob05re2img01.jpg", "id": 0, "text": "<span class=\"strong\"> Jason:</span> I have to prepare a presentation about one type of storage, and I was wondering if you could help me. You are known for being an expert with computers. <br/><span class=\"strong\"> Barb:</span> Sure, what type of storage do you want to talk about? <br/><span class=\"strong\"> Jason:</span> I'm not sure. Can you talk to me a little about each type? <br/><span class=\"strong\"> Barb:</span> Well, I can think of four types. Magnetic storage, which is used to record and read digital content in a magnetic form; optical storage, which is used with discs and laser technologies; solid-state storage, which is about portable devices; and finally, cloud storage, which is related to an online service with a network memory that you can expand. All of them were designed as non-volatile memories due to the fact that volatile memories are intended to clear all data when the power gets off."}, {"time": "48000", "image": "enpe8n6le01ob05re2img02.jpg", "id": 1, "text": "<span class=\"strong\"> Jason:</span> Can you give me more information about optical storage? That one sounds interesting. <br/>\n<span class=\"strong\"> Barb:</span> First you need to understand the difference between disc and disk. Discs were created to read and write information through a laser.  They can handle a high-capacity storage in different formats, and the data is more durable since it is difficult for them to record errors. Besides, the information is more secure. That's what I can tell you about optical storage. <br/>"}, {"time": "75600", "image": "enpe8n6le01ob05re2img03.jpg", "id": 2, "text": "<span class=\"strong\"> Jason:</span> And what is a disk?\n<br/>\n<span class=\"strong\"> Barb:</span> Disks were made for magnetic storage. Magnetic storage has a large-capacity to file data provide rapid access to the user. Before, the most common device was the floppy disk but now we have hard drives, you can use them in laptops or desktop computers. Unfortunately magnetic storage devices can be easily destroyed or infected by virus. <br/>\n<span class=\"strong\"> Jason:</span> I guess I will choose the optical storage then."}], "coverimg": "enpe8n6le01ob05re2img01.jpg", "audiosrc": "enpe8n6le01ob05re2aud01"}, "type": "slideshow"}], "type": "audio", "_data": [], "id": 1, "title": ""}], "exercises": [{"stimuli_ids": [0], "template_override": 1, "questions": [], "type": "WLC", "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": "I can talk about different types of storage."}, {"type": "Learnin